From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:50:33 +0200
Subject: media: sun6i-isp: Report what the demosaic measured

The demosaic reports two things, and neither reaches userspace. It
overwrites the minimum RGB field of its own configuration register with
the minimum it saw -- the vendor's 3A loop reads that every frame -- and
it writes a texture measure into CFA_TEX, which the vendor exports a
getter for and never calls.

Both live in the save region rather than the statistics DMA, so they can
only be had by reading back what the hardware wrote over the
configuration. That is available through debugfs, but only between
captures, where it races runtime suspend. Put them in the statistics
buffer instead, where they arrive with the frame they belong to.

The demosaic has no enable bit, so they are always reported.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_reg.h   |  1 +
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_stats.c | 13 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_reg.h b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_reg.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_reg.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_reg.h
@@ -387,6 +387,7 @@
 #define SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG0_REG			0x154
 #define SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG0_DIR_TH(v)		((v) & GENMASK(12, 0))
 #define SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG0_MIN_RGB(v)		(((v) << 16) & GENMASK(25, 16))
+#define SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG0_MIN_RGB_GET(v)	(((v) & GENMASK(25, 16)) >> 16)
 
 /*
  * The minimum goes into three fields across two registers, the same value
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_stats.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_stats.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_stats.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_stats.c
@@ -96,6 +96,19 @@ static void sun6i_isp_stats_buffer_fill(struct sun6i_isp_device *isp_dev,
 		blocks |= SUN6I_ISP_STAT_AWB;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The demosaic has no enable bit and always runs, and it reports by
+	 * overwriting its own configuration in the save region rather than
+	 * through the statistics DMA -- so this comes from there, not from
+	 * `base`.
+	 */
+	stats->cfa.min_rgb =
+		SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG0_MIN_RGB_GET(sun6i_isp_save_read(isp_dev,
+						SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG0_REG));
+	stats->cfa.texture = sun6i_isp_save_read(isp_dev,
+						 SUN6I_ISP_CFA_TEX_REG);
+	blocks |= SUN6I_ISP_STAT_CFA;
+
 	stats->blocks_valid = blocks;
 }
 
